            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Take your correct standing desk height — elbows at roughly ninety degrees, shoulders relaxed, wrists flat — and add the thickness of the walking pad deck, typically four to six inches. That total is the minimum the work surface must physically reach. Many popular adjustable desks top out just short of it for taller users, which is the single most common reason a treadmill desk gets abandoned.",
