        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Do the height arithmetic first: <strong class="text-white">your correct standing desk
            height plus the deck thickness</strong> is the number your desk must reach. Get that
            wrong and the setup produces neck pain and gets abandoned within a month, whatever you
            spent on the pad.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Build it as a walking pad under an adjustable desk rather than as an all-in-one, keep the
            ability to sit, attach walking to calls and reading rather than to a daily target, and
            start at twenty minutes. Then treat it as replacing sitting —
            <a href="/treadmill-workouts/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">real sessions</a>
            are a separate thing, and you want both.
          </p>
        </div>
